# Target C-II — lift the orbit/detour floor to the full-core loaded surplus

**Date:** 2026-09-14  
**Repository base:** `046784db`  
**Status:** proved proof-only consequence; theorem-state authority unchanged  
**Scope:** canonical full-core, no-macroscopic-container, near-disk Type-II branch  
**Dependencies:** canonical loaded-chord elimination and component deatomization; proof-only AG42/§171 orbit-diameter refinement

## LEVEL I STATUS

`STILL OPEN`

The AG42 refinement of the audited §171 orbit/detour theorem gives, at proof-only scope,

\[
\liminf_{D\to\infty}{q-k\over D}
\ge t_{42}:=C_{146}+0.0013751
>1.82088863795,
\]

where

\[
C_{146}={4\over9}\left(\pi+\sqrt{\Delta_2}\right),
\qquad
\Delta_2={\pi\over2\sqrt3}.
\]

In the canonical full-core Type-II branch, the promoted loaded-chord theorem and component deatomization turn this directly into a stronger floor for

\[
\mu_D={e_{BB}+2s_C-3k\over D}.
\]

This consequence was not recorded in the existing AG42 or correlated-train notes.

## 1. Exact loaded-chord identity

Canonical loaded-chord elimination gives, for every sufficiently large full-core representative,

\[
c_B=0,
\qquad e_{BB}=q-m_B,
\]

and the exact finite identity

\[
\boxed{\mu_DD=q+m_B-k-2c_I-4.}
\tag{OL.1}
\]

Here `m_B>=0` is the number of nonunit loaded-force-hull sides and `c_I` is the number of unloaded positive-contact components. Canonical all-phase component deatomization gives

\[
c_I=O(D^{2/3})=o(D).
\tag{OL.2}
\]

Therefore

\[
\mu_D
={q-k\over D}+{m_B\over D}-o(1)
\ge {q-k\over D}-o(1).
\tag{OL.3}
\]

No endpoint assumption on `m_B` is used.

## 2. Lift of the AG42/§171 floor

The proof-only AG42/§171 refinement gives the safe certified value

\[
\liminf {q-k\over D}
\ge C_{146}+0.0013751,
\]

with

\[
1.8208886379510192
<C_{146}+0.0013751
<1.8208886379954636.
\]

Combining with (OL.3) yields

\[
\boxed{
\liminf_{D\to\infty}\mu_D
\ge C_{146}+0.0013751
>1.82088863795.
}
\tag{OL.4}
\]

This strictly supersedes, for the full-core branch, the direct correlated-train surplus floor

\[
\liminf\mu_D\ge1.785463210824532\ldots.
\]

The numerical gain is more than `0.0354254`. The correlated-train theorem remains essential: its endpoint handshake supplies the stronger structural lower bounds on `J_D`, exceptional faces, chamber perimeter/slack, and the linear rhombus-count deficit. Equation (OL.4) only strengthens the scalar `mu_D` consequence.

## 3. Scope and frontier effect

This is not a C-II closure theorem.

- The AG42 constant `0.00042` is still proof-only pending independent audit, so (OL.4) inherits that lifecycle status.
- The lift uses the canonical full-core loaded-chord identity. It does not apply to the separate macroscopic inactive-container branch.
- There is no known upper bound on `mu_D` below `1.82088863795...`; increasing `m_B` only increases `mu_D` in (OL.1).
- The result supplies no same-cardinality strict sub-`D` competitor and forces no exact unit equilateral triangle.

The useful structural message is that the surviving full-core branch is already in a high-loaded-surplus regime. Future scalar regressions should impose (OL.4), not the older `mu_TC=1.63756...` or `1.78546...` floors.

## 4. Reproducibility

Run

```bash
python3 research/verify_target_c_orbit_loaded_surplus_floor.py
python3 research/verify_target_c_orbit_detour_gap_00042.py
```

The first script checks only the constant propagation. The second is the existing outward exact-rational certificate for the AG42/§171 endpoint.
